    <statement><p>Let <m>f</m> be a differentiable function of <m>x</m> 
(whose formula is not known)
and recall that <m>\frac{d}{dx}[f(x)]</m> and <m>f'(x)</m> 
are interchangeable notations. Using the <m>f'</m> notation, determine the
following derivative in terms of <m>x</m> and the 
unknown function <m>f</m>.</p>
<p>Be sure to type the multiplication symbol between variables or constants and <m>f</m> or <m>f'</m>.</p>
<p><m>\frac{d}{dx}[x^{2}+f\mathopen{}\left(x\right)] =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{d}{dx}[x^{2}f\mathopen{}\left(x\right)] =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{d}{dx}[c+x+\left(f\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)^{2}] =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{d}{dx}[f\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}\right)] =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{d}{dx}[xf\mathopen{}\left(x\right)+f\mathopen{}\left(cx\right)+cf\mathopen{}\left(x\right)] =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2x+f'\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2xf\mathopen{}\left(x\right)+x^{2}f'\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1+2f\mathopen{}\left(x\right)f'\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2xf'\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>f\mathopen{}\left(x\right)+xf'\mathopen{}\left(x\right)+cf'\mathopen{}\left(cx\right)+cf'\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
